WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.916
A star that blew up.

00:02.616 --> 00:05.104
A heavy star ends differently.

00:05.554 --> 00:09.101
Its core collapses and the rest is blown into space.

00:09.551 --> 00:19.878
People saw this one happen: in the year 1054 Chinese astronomers recorded a new star that could be seen in daylight for nearly a month.

00:20.328 --> 00:23.202
This is the wreck today, the Crab Nebula.
